      "id": "GENUS_JACANA",
      "name": "Jacana",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A genus of two tropical jacana species found in the Americas, known for their elaborate facial wattles and frontal shields. Like all jacanas, they have extraordinarily long toes and claws that allow them to walk across floating vegetation, a behaviour that earned them the colloquial name 'lily-trotters'.",
